{
  "id": "primacy-effect",
  "term": "primacy effect",
  "definition": "In auditory perception, the primacy effect is the tendency for the earliest parts of a sound to have more influence on judged loudness than later parts. This influence decreases over time, so the beginning of a time-varying sound is weighted more heavily than its later portions.",
